{
  "name": "Odynza Radar Signals",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## Odynza Radar Signals (M0 competitor intelligence)\nBuilt-in nodes only, no Code nodes.\n\n1. Open each **Gemini** model node → Credential → *Google Gemini(PaLM) Api* → the same key as the Strategy and Content workflows.\n2. Click **Publish** (activate) so both webhooks are live: `/webhook/radar-signals` and `/webhook/radar-weekly`.\n3. Optional: if Radar's .env has `N8N_SHARED_TOKEN`, put the same value in **both Settings nodes → radar_token**.\n\n**Top row (after every collection):** Radar found changes by rules (no AI). Classify names each change; Impact scores it 1–5 against the client profile, using the client's own corrections as examples, and writes what it means for the client.\n\n**Bottom row (Sunday night, or \"Make brief now\"):** Brief picks 3–7 items from the week (never padded), Claims maps who claims what, Opportunities ranks openings with all 10 fields. Radar checks everything before saving."
      },
